## 7. Milestones

| M | Scope | Files | Exit criterion |
|---|---|---|---|
| **M0** | Value-type catalog, acceptors, shape classes, type-aware equality | `value_types.py` (new) | Unit tests per type; `_matches` → `vtype.equal` with old URL behaviour preserved for `URL`. |
| **M1** | Typed extraction + capacity ledger | `tools.py`, `prompts.py`, `claude.py`/`opencua.py`/`uitars.py`, `tool_registry.py`, `screen_labels.py` | A `BOOL`/`ENUM`/`PACKAGE_NAME` query returns a validated value at `COMPUTED_PLATFORM_VALUE`, shown in the clear; malformed answers fail closed; bits accrue in `declass_log.jsonl` and a budget can block. |
| **M2** | Verifier framework + `task_match`, `candidate_set`, `registry` | `declassify.py`, `policies.TOOL_TIER`, `loop.py:398` (thread the instruction) | §6.1 and §6.3 pass end-to-end benign; their adversarial variants still block. |
| **M2b** | Screen channel: `locate` (deterministic) + `screen_attests` + localisation labelling | `locate.py` (new), `tools.py`, `tool_registry.py`, `screen_labels.py` (reuse `region_metadata`) | §6.8 clicks the unique row and refuses the ambiguous one; a hallucinated read fails `screen_attests`; a located answer carries its node's label instead of the whole-screen join. |
| **M3a** | Episode capability derivation + AST parse/classify/contain | `episode_capabilities.py` (new, modeled on `trust_detection.py`), `recipes.py` (new), `capabilities.py` (AST-based classification) | §6.3's injected `rm` and §6.5's `.zshrc` write rejected at extraction; benign halves unaffected. |
| **M3b** | The escape ladder — playbooks, Tier B constraints, Tier C structural crosscheck, argv rendering, `run_recipe` | `recipes.py`, `hybrid_tools.py`, `policies.py` (op-derived tier) | §6.4 passes benign *including* `curl \| sudo bash`; the appended-stage variant is rejected structurally. |
| **M4** | Audit + analysis | `declassify.py`, `test/sa_offline.py` | Per-episode bits, verifier mix, type distribution, block reasons summarized offline. |
| **M5** | Evaluation | `evaluation_examples/*` | Benign success + adversarial robustness per family vs. the current agent; over-blocking measured under `--sa_policy_mode audit`. |

M0–M2 are independently useful and don't touch Layer 3. M3a is the security core; M3b is what makes families 5–6 actually pass.

